WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.868
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:04.000
You have a great mustache.
-Thank you.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.534
It's actually, it's --

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.467
it's quite versatile,
I've discovered,

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:10.000
because it's, you know,
when I'm dressed nicely,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.000
it's very English.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.133
It's very erudite.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:14.000
But if I'm in jeans
and a T-shirt,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.400
I'm Schneider
from "One Day at a Time."

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.434
You know I mean because it's...
[ Laughs ]

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:18.434
-Of course. Yeah.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:19.734
Do people
recognize you?

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.267
No, it's quite --
It's an amazing disguise.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:22.767
It's like Clark Kent
with the glasses, right?

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:24.567
It's all the takes. It's just --
And no one knows him.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:25.734
-Yeah, that always
made me wonder.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.200
-I just -- I just did my thin
little mustache,

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.868
and I smiled at people
who I think recognize me,

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:31.834
and they're like,
"Ew, that guy..."

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.634
"That guy makes porn
in his basement or something"

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.467
-[ Laughter ]
-You know?

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:39.467
-I think
the first time we met

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.033
was when you hosted
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:42.400
-Yeah.
-And you were fantastic.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.634
Well, you were a great host.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.167
-21 years ago.
-That was 21...?

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:46.701
-Uh-huh, I know.
We've been friends for 21 years.

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:49.467
Do you remember the musical
guest when you hosted?

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:51.434
-Yeah, it's
a little embarrassing.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:55.901
My musical guest
was Jay-Z and Beyoncé.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.801
Yeah. This was -- This is...

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.734
-Yeah, there's --
there's me at the end there.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:02.534
And I'm --
My musical knowledge

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:04.701
sort of died
with Freddie Mercury.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:08.100
So I -- I came on, I said,
"Who's my guest?"

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.734
And they said, "Jay."
And I went, "Wow.

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:12.734
Now Beyoncé, she's in --
she's in that girl group.

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:14.434
What does Mr. Z do?"

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:15.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:17.167
-Mr. Z.
-I'm really to this day,

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.267
very embarrassed about it.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:20.834
-Is that the --
That's an amazing show.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.100
-[ Laughs ]
-That was fantastic.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.667
-And you and I
had a sketch together

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.667
I was just
reminding you of before.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.601
He does this
radio morning jock.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:29.901
[ Nasally voice ]
And he does this voice.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:30.901
The man on the box.
-[ Nasally voice ] Absolutely.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.067
Yeah, what do you, yeah.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.467
-Let's -- Let's talk
to the man on the box.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:35.334
-[ Normal voice ]
Yeah, we did all these bits.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:36.868
By the way,
I've been loving the podcast.

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.501
Speaking of radio.
The podcast you do with Sean.

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:39.501
-[ Normal voice ]
Oh, with Sean, yeah.

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:40.501
-Sean Hayes.

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:41.501
I just --
-It's called just --

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.033
It's called
"Just Jack &amp; Will."

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.667
And it's about a show
that I'm not going to talk about

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:47.901
because out of respect
for -- for the strike we're on.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.501
But it is -- the pod--

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:50.968
They'd allowed us
to talk about the podcast

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:53.467
and it's so much fun to be back
with my old buddy Sean.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.200
-You're so funny together.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.334
And it's basically
talking about episodes.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:01:59.834
But you --

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.234
-Well, he got --
So this is crazy.

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:02.467
We were at lunch one day
and he said,

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.734
"We should do a podcast
about maybe the show."

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:06.300
And I said,
"Well, great."

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.968
Because I still watch it
all the time.

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.501
I can talk with
with tremendous fluency.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:13.033
And he said, "I've never --
I've never watched it."

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:14.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.434
I said,
You've never watched it?!"

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.601
So -- so here I am,
I'm rewatching.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:21.067
And he's -- he's like
someone with amnesia.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.334
It's like I --
-Yeah, he's seeing it...

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.934
-We were gay, best friends!

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.033
-It's so funny.

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:29.901
And gosh, you guys
have just, like, the timing

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:32.234
because obviously you worked
together for so long.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:33.467
-It's an old belt.
-It's just --

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:34.901
-Oh, it's unbelievable.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.234
Congrats on "The Cottage,"
by the way.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:37.667
-Thank you.
It has been so exciting.

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:40.501
We've been running
since early July and it is.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:43.033
Folks, when you leave here,
get a ticket.

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:44.234
It's really fun.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.567
It's through October 29th
at the Hayes Theater.

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:49.868
And I got to say, you got
one of the biggest honors ever

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.000
that I'm always --
I go there all the time.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.334
But Sardi's...
-Yeah.

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:56.400
-...is a restaurant
in the theater district.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.000
-Right beside our theater
and famous

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.634
for the caricatures on the wall,
some of them dating back

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:03.133
so far, you don't even
know who they are.

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:04.334
You can't read
the signature, but...

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:05.968
-Yeah.
-But, yeah, I was -- I got one.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:08.367
I got one a few weeks ago.
-This is a big deal.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.067
I want to show
the picture of you and you.

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:14.100
This is at Sardi's.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.067
Not bad. It looks good.
-It's not bad.

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:18.667
There's so many
pictures that you can't --

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:20.901
you can't figure how is there --
how's there room for me.

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:22.734
I would come in most nights
after the show,

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:25.534
and the very elegant maitre d'
would say, "Soon is your turn."

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:27.634
And then three days before,
he said,

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:30.267
"Any day now you
will be right here.

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:31.834
And I said, "Here,
like, right here

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:32.968
in the front foyer, the front?"

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:34.968
He said, "Yes."
I said, "For how long?"

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:36.000
He said,
"About a week."

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.467
-I'll take it. You go.
-Yeah, yeah, I...

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:39.934
-I'll take it.
Yeah, why not?

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.167
But you're being directed by

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.501
the one and only
Jason Alexander.

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.801
-Yes.
-Who is -- Who is...

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.067
-Obviously a legend.
-...the funniest.

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:49.334
-But also an old friend,
not from -- from NBC,

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:50.501
not from sitcom days.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:54.000
But we were dads
at the same school

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.434
and we used
to do parents nights

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:58.100
and we'd perform ridiculous
things with other dads.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.501
Nowadays, this school has,

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:03.467
like Dave Grohl and Beck
are dads, you know.

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:06.133
But back then it was -- it was
Jason and I and Steve Carell.

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:08.367
It was -- it was -- it was
sitcom dads, basically.

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:09.968
-But now --
now you're rocking out.

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:11.300
-Yeah, we're rocking out.
-Now you have rock performances.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.100
-And he has -- he has directed
the hell out of this.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.667
It is really hilarious.
-Oh, he's so funny.

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:18.334
What is -- what is CADs, though?
Can you explain what this is?

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:19.901
-Oh, boy.
They're going to kill me.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:22.601
CADs are just
a bunch of pals

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:25.033
that we've all worked
together or known.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:28.267
Richard Kind and Bryan Cranston
and Steven Weber

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.701
and Spencer Garrett.
There's Noah Wyle.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:32.501
And we just slowly but surely,
over the last few years,

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.200
before COVID
and then through COVID,

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.501
we get on Zoom
and eat together on Zoom.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.667
It's just a -- it's just
a bunch of dining.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:40.701
This is a great --
It's like a who's who.

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.000
This is super fun.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.667
-It's -- It's an amazing
group of guys.

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:46.467
But now it's even grown even --
These are more,

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:47.834
These are more CADs.
Who are these?

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.334
-More, CADs, yeah.
Who else we got there?

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:51.334
-That's LeVar Burton.
-That's LeVar Burton.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:52.534
Laurence Fishburne is there.

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:54.567
-Alfred Molina.
-Alfred Molina. It's...

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:57.133
-I want to be at this --
this lunch.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:59.234
You're not going to --
It's a very tough ticket.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:00.701
Very...
-Okay, I understand.

00:05:00.701 --> 00:05:04.100
I understand. I understand.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.601
-When you do "The Cottage,"
by the way,

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:07.100
I wanted to ask this because --

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.601
Do you know
if anyone's in the audience,

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:10.400
if someone's coming to see you
or if they're a celebrity or...?

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.767
-Well, some of those guys
came opening night,

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:13.534
but other nights,
I don't generally

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:15.300
find out until after.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.534
It's crazy, I have three
and a half years of COVID.

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:19.234
I never got it.
Never.

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:21.868
And then I've had it twice
in the run of this show.

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:23.367
Twice in the summer.
No.

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:27.100
And I very virtually
no symptoms,

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.868
but still had to take
five days off

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:30.067
and still had
to follow the protocol.

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:31.400
-Absolutely, Sure.
-So my understudy went on.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:34.200
He was great, but the second
time I was like, "Ugh."

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.334
And that night my understudy
went on for the second time,

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:37.834
Pierce Brosnan
showed up.

00:05:37.834 --> 00:05:38.834
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:41.601
And I was just like,
"Zewh! Really?!"

00:05:41.601 --> 00:05:42.701
-Yeah, He's James Bond?

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:44.200
-And somebody said,
"Just --

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.834
If you ever run into Pierce,
just tell him it was you.

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:46.834
He won't remember."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.834 --> 00:05:48.334
-Yeah. No.

00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:50.801
Can we say -- talk about what
"The Cottage" is about, please?

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:53.234
This is a -- it's a new play

00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:55.767
by a young American woman
named Sandy Rustin.

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:59.434
And, yet, it is 100 years old.
It takes place in 1923.

00:05:59.434 --> 00:06:01.067
It's an English cottage.

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:03.367
And all these couples
are cheating on

00:06:03.367 --> 00:06:04.634
each other
with each other.

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:07.300
It's a classic
British sex farce.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.234
[ Laughter ]
And it's -- Yeah.

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:12.033
And it's --
My cast is incredible.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:15.634
Just all Broadway vets and --
and Alex Moffat

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:17.801
from "SNL." Yes.
-Oh, from "SNL."

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:19.367
Oh, I love Alex Moffat.
-Alex and I play brothers.

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:21.067
He's got an even
bigger mustache.

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:22.501
-No way.
Please give him my best.

00:06:22.501 --> 00:06:23.734
-I absolutely will.
He's brilliant.

00:06:23.734 --> 00:06:25.267
-And I know that you're
a busy doing the show.

00:06:25.267 --> 00:06:26.501
You're going to go right
from here to the show.

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:28.300
It means so much to me

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.868
that you came on the show.
-It means so much to be asked.

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:31.000
-I love you, buddy.
-It's nice to see you

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.000
after all this time.
-Congratulations.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.467
-Thank you.
-And break a leg.

00:06:33.467 --> 00:06:34.834
-Come and see it, 3 more weeks.
-Talented dude right there.

00:06:34.834 --> 00:06:36.501
Eric McCormack, everyone.

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:38.467
"The Cottage" is running now

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:41.267
through October 29th
at the Hayes Theater.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
- We'll be right back.

00:06:42.634 --> 00:06:43.634
Stick around, everybody.

